{"id":12026,"date":"2025-04-15T23:23:52","date_gmt":"2025-04-15T23:23:52","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/?p=12026"},"modified":"2025-10-13T00:05:08","modified_gmt":"2025-10-13T00:05:08","slug":"living-throug-a-remodel","status":"publish","type":"post","link":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/living-throug-a-remodel\/","title":{"rendered":"Living Through a Sizable Remodel? The Best Ways to Stay Sane"},"content":{"rendered":"\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Embarking on a remodeling project can be both exciting and stressful. While the thought of transforming your home is thrilling, the reality of living amidst construction can test anyone\u2019s patience. At Harris &amp; Sons, we\u2019ve helped countless Oregon homeowners navigate this challenging period with ease. This guide provides practical tips to help you maintain your sanity during a remodel.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">However, you are looking for a more in-depth and personal discussion with our team regarding your specific project, feel free to book a hassle free, no obligation 1 on 1 virtual consultation with our Construction Consultant:<a href=\"https:\/\/api.leadconnectorhq.com\/widget\/bookings\/harris-sons-virtual-consultation\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" title=\"\">&nbsp;<strong>Book a Call.<\/strong><\/a><\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/AD_4nXdp-86ddh5f6pFFbUDq1ABgy4mRhRtcCkT1y63Wk-LmRcvTpKE6KE03TVWN0ywqmjPc4lXmskZnxhBTG_lCUdN_1T7Q8cImrh3YNrd2s3_cCb5gOUx58yI3AzTb1NzXE4KhRIcO4g.png\" alt=\"living through a remodel\" class=\"wp-image-12030\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>1. Set Clear Expectations<\/strong> Before Living Through a Remodel<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Before construction begins, ensure you understand the scope and timeline of the project. Having a detailed plan in place helps avoid surprises.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">\u2022 <strong>Pro Tip:<\/strong> Work with your contractor to establish a daily work schedule, including start and end times.<br>\u2022 <strong>Fact:<\/strong> According to the National Association of the Remodeling Industry (<a href=\"https:\/\/www.naripacificnw.org\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NARI<\/a>), clear communication reduces project delays by 30%.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>2. Designate a Construction-Free Zone<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Create a space in your home where you can escape the noise and chaos. This area should be clean, comfortable, and free from construction activity.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">\u2022 <strong>Example:<\/strong> A family in Oregon turned their guest bedroom into a temporary sanctuary during their kitchen remodel, complete with a coffee maker and mini-fridge.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>3. Plan for Temporary Adjustments<\/strong> While Living Through a Remodel<\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Also, key areas like the kitchen or bathroom are under renovation, make arrangements to minimize disruptions.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">\u2022 <strong>Kitchen Remodel Tips:<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Set up a temporary kitchen with essentials like a microwave, toaster oven, and mini-fridge.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use disposable plates and utensils to reduce cleanup.<br>\u2022 <strong>Bathroom Remodel Tips:<\/strong><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Coordinate shower times if sharing a bathroom.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Consider renting a portable bathroom for large-scale projects.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>4. Communicate Regularly with Your Contractor<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Regular updates from your contractor can provide peace of mind. Schedule weekly check-ins to discuss progress, address concerns, and make necessary adjustments.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">\u2022 <strong>Pro Tip:<\/strong> Use apps like Trello or Buildertrend to stay informed and track progress in real-time.<br>\u2022 <strong>Statistic:<\/strong> Projects with frequent client-contractor communication are 25% more likely to stay on schedule. (<a href=\"https:\/\/www.houzz.com\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Houzz<\/a>)<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>5. Manage Dust and Noise<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Construction dust and noise can be overwhelming, but there are ways to minimize their impact:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">\u2022 <strong>Dust Management:<\/strong><\/p>\n\n\n\n<ul class=\"wp-block-list\">\n<li>Use plastic sheeting to seal off construction areas.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Request air filters or purifiers to keep dust levels low.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Cover furniture and flooring in adjacent rooms.<br>\u2022 <strong>Noise Reduction:<\/strong><\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Schedule noisy work for times when you\u2019re not home.<\/li>\n\n\n\n<li>Use noise-canceling headphones or white noise machines.<\/li>\n<\/ul>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>6. Stick to Your Daily Routine<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Maintaining normalcy can help reduce stress. Stick to regular meal times, exercise routines, and family activities whenever possible.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">\u2022 <strong>Example:<\/strong> A Oregon couple continued their weekly movie nights by setting up a temporary TV area in their basement during their living room remodel.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>7. Prepare for the Unexpected<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Remodeling often comes with surprises, like delays or unforeseen issues. Preparing emotionally and financially for these challenges can make them easier to handle.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">\u2022 <strong>Pro Tip:<\/strong> Set aside 15-20% of your budget for contingencies.<br>\u2022 <strong>Fact:<\/strong> Remodeling projects encounter unexpected expenses in 37% of cases. (<a href=\"https:\/\/www.nahb.org\/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">NAHB<\/a>)<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>8. Take Breaks from the Chaos<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Don\u2019t hesitate to step away from the construction site. Spend time outdoors, visit friends, or treat yourself to a staycation.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">\u2022 <strong>Example:<\/strong> One Oregon family took a weekend getaway during their bathroom remodel, returning to significant progress and a refreshed mindset.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>9. Celebrate Small Wins<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Acknowledge milestones during the project to keep morale high. Celebrate the completion of key phases, like demolition or framing.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">\u2022 <strong>Pro Tip:<\/strong> Take photos throughout the process to document progress and stay motivated.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>10. Work with a Trusted Contractor<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Partnering with an experienced and reliable contractor like Harris &amp; Sons makes all the difference. We prioritize clear communication, efficient timelines, and minimizing disruptions for homeowners.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">\u2022 <strong>Case Study:<\/strong> During a basement remodel in Oregon, we provided weekly updates, handled dust control, and helped the family create a temporary workspace. The project finished on time and within budget, earning rave reviews.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<figure class=\"wp-block-image\"><img decoding=\"async\" src=\"https:\/\/landobuilderscorp.com\/wp-content\/uploads\/2025\/02\/AD_4nXfL2ajs_97nX2lzdqVPItssrLiT66FytxmtJHQ3X5mks6Qst9FqeBXVGx0sb0-A2jmXzJempEgo8NC15Fb8YXLrLV02Nj7JEXabbKI8q8wsqntaltDM2_1iTyBeCa1QS5DaVg6hSg.jpg\" alt=\"hire a expert remodeling company\" class=\"wp-image-12029\"\/><\/figure>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>11. How the Preconstruction Process Can Help While Living Through A Remodel<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Our Oregon Preconstruction Process offered by Harris &amp; Sons is designed to minimize stress and prevent surprises during your remodel. Here\u2019s how it can help:<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">\u2022 <strong>Detailed Planning:<\/strong> Our process includes thorough inspections to identify potential issues before construction begins, saving you time and money.<br>\u2022 <strong>Accurate Budgeting:<\/strong> By analyzing every aspect of the project, we provide a clear and realistic budget that reduces the risk of hidden costs.<br>\u2022 <strong>Streamlined Communication:<\/strong> We establish clear timelines, milestones, and regular updates to keep you informed at every step.<br>\u2022 <strong>Reduced Disruptions:<\/strong> From coordinating schedules to managing permits, our preconstruction process ensures a smoother, more efficient remodeling experience.<br>\u2022 <strong>Enhanced Comfort While Living Onsite:<\/strong> Preconstruction planning identifies and mitigates challenges like dust control, noise reduction, and temporary living adjustments.<br>\u2022 <strong>Optimized Use of Space:<\/strong> Design solutions created during preconstruction maximize functionality even during construction phases.<br>\u2022 <strong>Quick Issue Resolution:<\/strong> Anticipating potential challenges allows for faster problem-solving, minimizing downtime.<br>\u2022 <strong>Improved Safety:<\/strong> Preconstruction ensures hazardous areas are clearly identified and secured, keeping your family safe.<br>\u2022 <strong>Predictable Outcomes:<\/strong> Detailed preplanning reduces uncertainties, keeping the project on schedule and on budget.<br>\u2022 <strong>Personalized Solutions:<\/strong> The process allows us to tailor the remodel to your lifestyle needs, ensuring a better experience throughout.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">\u2022 <strong>Example:<\/strong> During a recent kitchen remodel, our preconstruction planning uncovered outdated wiring that could have delayed the project. By addressing it early, the homeowner avoided an extra $2,000 in unexpected costs and stayed on schedule.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Learn more about the Oregon Preconstruction Process here.<\/p>\n\n\n\n<hr class=\"wp-block-separator has-alpha-channel-opacity\"\/>\n\n\n\n<h2 class=\"wp-block-heading\"><strong>Final Thoughts<\/strong><\/h2>\n\n\n\n<p class=\"wp-block-paragraph\">Living through a remodel doesn\u2019t have to be overwhelming. By setting expectations, creating a construction-free zone, and working with a trusted contractor, you can navigate this period with ease. At Harris &amp; Sons, we\u2019re committed to making the remodeling process as stress-free as possible for Oregon homeowners. Our Oregon Preconstruction Process ensures you\u2019re prepared for every aspect of your remodel, from start to finish. <strong>Ready to start your dream remodel?<br><\/strong><a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/contact-us-2\/\" title=\"\">Contact Harris &amp; Sons<\/a> today to learn more about the Oregon Preconstruction Process and how we can transform your home.<br><a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/contact-us\/\" title=\"\">Get in Touch<\/a> | <a href=\"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/services\/\" title=\"\">Explore Our Services<\/a><\/p>\n","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"<p>Embarking on a remodeling project can be both exciting and stressful. While the thought of transforming your home is thrilling, the reality of living amidst construction can test anyone\u2019s patience. At Harris &amp; Sons, we\u2019ve helped countless Oregon homeowners navigate this challenging period with ease. This guide provides practical tips to help you maintain your [&hellip;]<\/p>\n","protected":false},"author":1,"featured_media":12028,"comment_status":"open","ping_status":"open","sticky":false,"template":"","format":"standard","meta":{"_acf_changed":false,"footnotes":""},"categories":[36,32,38,33,39],"tags":[],"class_list":["post-12026","post","type-post","status-publish","format-standard","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","category-general","category-kitchen-resources","category-remodel","category-remodeling-tips","category-resources"],"acf":[],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/12026","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/post"}],"author":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/users\/1"}],"replies":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/comments?post=12026"}],"version-history":[{"count":6,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/12026\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":15226,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/posts\/12026\/revisions\/15226"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=12026"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/categories?post=12026"},{"taxonomy":"post_tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/harrisandsons.co\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/tags?post=12026"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}